 the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$\n- **II.** $A$ is invertible\n- **III.** $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Given a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f00f19b1-a5d9-5f3f-892f-2e3d8e66d32c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450566} {:answer/id #uuid "f24b70da-3d6e-5768-987e-5a6a1111b77e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f00f19b1-a5d9-5f3f-892f-2e3d8e66d32c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450566} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac17f050-593c-55c0-be4c-979e6666933f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451237} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40c3344c-65d7-58be-ae26-42bb9b9f586a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450568} {:answer/id #uuid "740835e0-32e5-50d4-b9e7-dfc4013e2ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "740835e0-32e5-50d4-b9e7-dfc4013e2ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450569} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0e7cf2e-0dcc-5b45-a214-fc4802e94260" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451238} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f9e3557-049b-5e3a-bce9-8906dde445a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450570} {:answer/id #uuid "9efcb6d2-5f9b-556f-ba0b-a54c998fb8e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f9e3557-049b-5e3a-bce9-8906dde445a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450570} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fd7516a-09ae-5918-99f5-dc75f2fb3320" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b252a44d-8417-5bdc-8a9b-ad6e81276b7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-36075" :question/problem "Let \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(A)=0$\n- **II.** $Ax=0$ has the unique  solution $⟨0,0⟩$\n- **III.** $⟨5,-4⟩$ is a solution to $Ax=0$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-6\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement II is true by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false. Again,  according to the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, the system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054632 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "495f3da0-849a-589d-ac88-26d6825445e4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Subsets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a318415-af17-5fcb-90b3-4e147fe1e830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450572} {:answer/id #uuid "12648c58-bd6b-5bfb-ba68-38821d15483a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a318415-af17-5fcb-90b3-4e147fe1e830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450572} :answer-field/id #uuid "13533289-5901-5512-b94b-2e7969173948" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451240} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df2cf1ee-6702-59fe-8e01-8d9293eb42db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450574} {:answer/id #uuid "9631eefa-83a6-5406-8ce1-0b4a0bf5727f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df2cf1ee-6702-59fe-8e01-8d9293eb42db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450574} :answer-field/id #uuid "111fb8ec-8507-5fc9-adc0-2a0d4fd97494" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451241} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc3ac701-f2b7-51d3-9617-126db7db1e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450576} {:answer/id #uuid "3d3fbad1-5c47-5cd3-ba33-710b96fa6475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d3fbad1-5c47-5cd3-ba33-710b96fa6475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450577} :answer-field/id #uuid "192cd3c4-7c44-5235-af6c-f4ef5919d344" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac28aad1-833b-50ff-aaf3-b0e247f97248" :question/math-academy-id "q-37260" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in N:3\\le x<9}$ and $B={x\\in N:3x<10}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A⊆B$\n- **II.** $B⊆A$\n- **III.** $∅⊆A$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all natural numbers greater than or equal to $3$ but less than $9.$ So,\n\n$$\nA={3,4,5,6,7,8}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are natural numbers which satisfy the inequality $3x<10.$ So,\n\n$$\nB={1,2,3}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false. For example, $4\\in A$ but $4\\notin B.$\n\n- $B⊆A$ is false. For example, $1\\in B$ but $1\\notin A.$\n\n- $∅⊆A$ is true. The null set $∅={}$ is a subset of *every* set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323894 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054632 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "495f3da0-849a-589d-ac88-26d6825445e4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Subsets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5ec21c1-52fd-5aea-87a3-631b1273b5d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450578} {:answer/id #uuid "11dfff47-9d8a-5144-956f-42e803ff6f4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5ec21c1-52fd-5aea-87a3-631b1273b5d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450578} :answer-field/id #uuid "a94ef6a1-baa2-5132-850f-574dc1956238" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/t