 {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450641} :answer-field/id #uuid "618ce025-20da-5809-a4f2-b304969686e3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca108716-0018-5080-8610-49601a0656af" :question/math-academy-id "q-42376" :question/problem "$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,F=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $D,E,$ and $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $ED$ is well defined\n- **II.** The product $FD$ is well defined\n- **III.** The product $EF$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, $E$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $F$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $E$ and $2$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ equals the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $E$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{D}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $F$ and $2$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $F$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $F$ and $D$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{F}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{D}_{2\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $E$ and $2$ rows in $F.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ equals the number of rows in $F,$ the matrices $E$ and $F$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{F}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca8eb228-c1aa-526c-bf90-27f66a9356c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450642} {:answer/id #uuid "bd87b62f-9da3-5f73-ab7a-d82a98e30bc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca8eb228-c1aa-526c-bf90-27f66a9356c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450642} :answer-field/id #uuid "75caa915-3858-5c01-a5f4-aac230541fcf" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451275} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df04892a-3fcd-5b6f-a931-273de40f055b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450644} {:answer/id #uuid "19d2a187-bbe2-537c-ac7f-4d7af02d3c9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19d2a187-bbe2-537c-ac7f-4d7af02d3c9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450645} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbdeb417-add7-50cd-8d61-987eb71ef15f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451276} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84322445-b037-524f-b315-0b6ef58f9865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450646} {:answer/id #uuid "8e92c41b-83e4-555c-ac78-30c970f6f412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e92c41b-83e4-555c-ac78-30c970f6f412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450647} :answer-field/id #uuid "27f9d256-723e-592c-9c15-bc392aa403f0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e41c04ee-99fe-56c1-8773-ea0949cc66d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-42377" :question/problem "$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,M=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,N=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $L,M,$ and $N?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $ML$ is well defined\n- **II.** The product $MN$ is well defined\n- **III.** The product $LN$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $L$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, $M$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $N$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $M$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $M$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $L,$ the matrices $M$ and $L$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{M}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{L}_{2\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $M$ and $3$ rows in $N.$ Since the number of columns in $M$ equals the number of rows in $N,$ the matrices $M$ and $N$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{M}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{N}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $L$ and $3$ rows in $N.$ Since the number of columns in $L$ equals the number of rows in $N,$ the matrices $L$ and $N$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{L}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{N}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are true, while statement I is false."}]}
